      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name means “union of lands,” reflecting its origin as a gathering of parcels when incorporated in 1734.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        16,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.ct.one/towns/union",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Union’s highest town center sits at 1,015 feet, the fourth highest in Connecticut, giving it a distinctive hilltop feel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Union%2C_Connecticut",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Union Free Public Library, opened in 1895 in a private home, remains one of the town’s few historic public buildings.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
